{"repo_id":"Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B","prompt":"The lighthouse keeper wrote in his log every evening, even when nothing happened. On the first of March the wind turned east and the fishing boats stayed in the harbour. On the second, a crate of oranges washed ashore, and the children of the village carried them up the hill in their sweaters. On the third, the lamp's clockwork slowed, so he oiled the gears and counted the seconds between flashes until they were even again. On the fourth, a letter arrived from his sister in Valparaíso asking whether the sea was still the same colour. He answered that it changed every hour, grey at dawn, green at noon, and almost black before a storm, and that he had stopped trying to name it. On the fifth, nothing happened, and he wrote that down too, because a quiet day was also worth remembering. By the end of the month the log held thirty-one entries, and he read them aloud to the gulls on the gallery rail.","input_token_ids":[760,324,55965,51624,5947,303,780,1433,1396,11129,11,1442,948,4161,6716,13,1848,279,1118,314,5297,279,9662,6316,10663,321,279,19340,30592,19013,303,279,72103,13,1848,279,2018,11,264,17189,314,81141,36251,23083,451,11,321,279,2748,314,279,13721,11354,1070,685,279,23198,303,836,10233,11203,13,1848,279,4688,11,279,27056,579,8598,1715,46251,11,748,551,296,2112,279,51373,321,29014,279,6283,1881,59215,2980,781,998,1442,1495,13,1848,279,11400,11,264,6321,11136,494,780,12553,303,3968,14365,204955,9859,3315,279,9117,557,1990,279,1788,12106,13,1216,18018,421,424,5324,1396,6258,11,19177,506,37119,11,5983,506,35915,11,321,4409,3565,1518,264,13071,11,321,421,551,995,10184,4313,310,803,424,13,1848,279,17175,11,4161,6716,11,321,551,5947,421,1441,2166,11,1521,264,11012,1834,557,1048,5621,45708,13,3113,279,809,314,279,2182,279,1433,5467,25292,18030,10379,11,321,551,1301,1070,68030,310,279,338,68042,383,279,17507,13176,13],"positions":[{"position":0,"top_indices":[2614,220,1414,3377,7193,1118,3049,328,7308,5839,3788,8358,4496,3274,1379